.class public final Lcom/box/app/vpn/VpnConfig;
.super Ljava/lang/Object;
.source "VpnConfig.java"

# Rewrites the user's proxy configuration so that the core can run as a plain,
# unprivileged child process.
#
# BoxProxy normally hands the core a "startup-config" generated by boxctl, and
# the user's own file is written for a rooted run mode: it enables TUN, binds
# TPROXY/REDIRECT ports, sets find-process-mode, routing marks, ... Every one of
# those needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and makes mihomo/sing-box abort immediately when
# they are started without root ("create tun: operation not permitted").
#
# sanitize() therefore produces a VPN flavour of the very same configuration:
#   * all root-only listeners are dropped / rewritten into a local SOCKS5 one
#   * that SOCKS5 listener always ends up on a known, free 127.0.0.1 port which
#     is then handed to hev-socks5-tunnel
# Everything else (proxies, proxy-groups, rules, providers, DNS) is untouched,
# so the user keeps their own routing policy.

.field public static final BASE_PORT:I = 0x45e2    # 17890


